From 6aac978e21a17e8d3809195903168309ffd309d4 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Huzefa Siamwala <huzefasid@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 15:20:16 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] feat(apps): a bot can be assigned its own connected account
 per app

A bot's new connectorAccounts setting names the connected account it uses for
an app, and can keep that account to itself (exclusive). The harness relay
writes the assigned account into every COMPOSIO_MULTI_EXECUTE_TOOL entry for
that app, whatever the model asked for, and refuses the call when the account
is no longer connected instead of falling back to another one. Other bots can
no longer name an exclusive account by ID or alias. Calls that cannot be read
(remote workbench, bash, proxy code, direct tool calls, batches) and
disconnecting an account through COMPOSIO_MANAGE_CONNECTIONS are refused while
account rules reach the bot. App-event automations follow the same choice, and
a bot a Chief creates inherits the Chief's assignment.

With no account assigned on any bot nothing changes. Bot Settings > Access
gets an Accounts list (owner/admin only on a Team Cloud).

Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01S7mkJCMRBgQyRQMomQYhKE
Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
